<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Assessment Marking Criteria Sheet — Year 10 Commerce</title>
  <!--[if gte mso 9]>
  <xml>
    <w:WordDocument>
      <w:View>Print</w:View>
      <w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom>
      <w:DoNotOptimizeForBrowser/>
    </w:WordDocument>
  </xml>
  <![endif]-->
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: 'Arial', 'Calibri', sans-serif;
      color: #1e293b;
      line-height: 1.4;
      font-size: 10pt;
      background: #ffffff;
    }
    .header {
      text-align: center;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #0f172a;
      padding-bottom: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
    }
    .header h1 {
      font-size: 15pt;
      margin: 0;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
      color: #0f172a;
    }
    .header h2 {
      font-size: 11pt;
      color: #475569;
      margin: 3px 0 0 0;
      font-weight: bold;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    table.meta-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      font-size: 9.5pt;
    }
    table.meta-table td {
      border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      background: #f8fafc;
    }
    .rubric-title {
      font-size: 11pt;
      font-weight: bold;
      color: #ffffff;
      background: #0f172a;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      border-radius: 3px;
      margin-top: 15px;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    table.rubric-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      font-size: 9pt;
    }
    table.rubric-table th, table.rubric-table td {
      border: 1px solid #94a3b8;
      padding: 6px 8px;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    table.rubric-table th {
      background: #f1f5f9;
      font-weight: bold;
      text-align: left;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-size: 8.5pt;
    }
    .bullets {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 12px;
      font-size: 8.5pt;
      color: #475569;
    }
    .score-cell {
      text-align: center;
      font-weight: bold;
      background: #f8fafc;
      vertical-align: middle;
      font-size: 10pt;
    }
    .grade-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      font-size: 8.5pt;
    }
    .grade-table th, .grade-table td {
      border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
      padding: 5px 8px;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    .grade-table th {
      background: #f8fafc;
      font-weight: bold;
      text-align: left;
    }
    .grade-cell {
      font-weight: bold;
      text-align: center;
      background: #f1f5f9;
      font-size: 10pt;
      vertical-align: middle;
    }
    .feedback-section {
      border: 1px solid #94a3b8;
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 10px;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      background: #f8fafc;
    }
    .feedback-title {
      font-weight: bold;
      font-size: 9.5pt;
      color: #0f172a;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
      padding-bottom: 3px;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .feedback-box {
      min-height: 55px;
      font-size: 9pt;
      color: #64748b;
    }
    .footer-signatures {
      width: 100%;
      margin-top: 15px;
      font-size: 9pt;
    }
    .page-break {
      page-break-before: always;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="header">
    <h1>STAGE 5 COMMERCE — ASSESSMENT MARKING CRITERIA SHEET</h1>
    <h2>Task 3: Travel Portfolio &amp; Contingency Plan (Total: 30 Marks)</h2>
  </div>

  <table class="meta-table">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 15%;"><strong>Student Name:</strong></td>
      <td style="width: 35%;">____________________________________</td>
      <td style="width: 18%;"><strong>Class / Teacher:</strong></td>
      <td style="width: 32%;">____________________</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Destination:</strong></td>
      <td>____________________________________</td>
      <td><strong>Final Score / Grade:</strong></td>
      <td><strong>        / 30   |   Grade: ______</strong></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div class="rubric-title">Detailed Marking Rubric</div>
  
  <table class="rubric-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 25%;">Component &amp; Outcomes</th>
        <th style="width: 23%;">High / Outstanding</th>
        <th style="width: 23%;">Sound / Substantial</th>
        <th style="width: 23%;">Basic / Limited</th>
        <th style="width: 6%;">Score</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <!-- Component A -->
      <tr>
        <td>
          <strong>Part A: Destination &amp; Sourced Itinerary</strong><br/>
          <span style="font-size: 8pt; color:#64748b;">(COM5-6, COM5-7)</span>
          <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top: 4px;">
            <li>7–10 day itinerary</li>
            <li>Cultural landmark/tour</li>
            <li>Comparative sourced quotes (flights &amp; accommodation)</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>7–8 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Realistic, logical 7–10 day itinerary tailored to the 18–25 age demographic. Meaningfully integrates at least one cultural site/experience. Sourced comparative flights &amp; accommodations with working links/clear screenshots.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>4–6 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Complete itinerary with logical travel connections and cultural site included. Sourced quotes included for flights &amp; accommodations with minor omissions in details or links. General demographic justification.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>1–3 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Incomplete or unrealistic itinerary schedule. Missing cultural site, comparative quotes, booking links, or screenshots. Superficial or missing target market rationale.</p>
        </td>
        <td class="score-cell">/ 8</td>
      </tr>

      <!-- Component B -->
      <tr>
        <td>
          <strong>Part B: Financial Budget Spreadsheet</strong><br/>
          <span style="font-size: 8pt; color:#64748b;">(COM5-1, COM5-4)</span>
          <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top: 4px;">
            <li>Itemised cost breakdown</li>
            <li>Foreign currency to AUD conversion</li>
            <li>5–10% buffer under $10,000</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>7–8 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Accurate, fully itemised budget covering transport, lodging, living, and pre-departure costs. Clear, accurate currency conversion formulas into AUD. Includes a calculated 5–10% contingency buffer strictly within the $10,000 cap.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>4–6 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Complete budget adhering to the $10,000 cap with minor costing omissions. Correct currency conversions with minor calculation errors. Emergency contingency buffer included.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>1–3 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Incomplete budget spreadsheet with major calculation/conversion errors. Omits major expense categories or exceeds the $10,000 AUD limit. Missing contingency buffer.</p>
        </td>
        <td class="score-cell">/ 8</td>
      </tr>

      <!-- Component C -->
      <tr>
        <td>
          <strong>Part C: Smartraveller, Laws &amp; Insurance</strong><br/>
          <span style="font-size: 8pt; color:#64748b;">(COM5-2, COM5-4)</span>
          <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top: 4px;">
            <li>DFAT advisory &amp; entry rules</li>
            <li>2 local laws &amp; 2 cultural customs</li>
            <li>Insurance quote comparison</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>7–8 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Accurate, detailed DFAT advisory level and passport/visa/vaccine entry requirements. Clear explanation of 2 specific local laws and 2 cultural customs/etiquette rules. Sourced insurance quotes with sound justification.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>4–6 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Accurate summary of DFAT advice level and entry rules. Identifies local laws and cultural customs. Includes sourced travel insurance comparison with basic justification.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>1–3 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Superficial or inaccurate DFAT advisory information. Incomplete coverage of local laws, customs, or insurance policies. Missing insurance quotes or sources.</p>
        </td>
        <td class="score-cell">/ 8</td>
      </tr>

      <!-- Component D -->
      <tr>
        <td>
          <strong>Part D: Emergency Crisis Management</strong><br/>
          <span style="font-size: 8pt; color:#64748b;">(COM5-5, COM5-8)</span>
          <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top: 4px;">
            <li>First 24-hour action steps</li>
            <li>Embassy role &amp; limitations</li>
            <li>Insurer claim &amp; emergency funds</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>5–6 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Highly logical, sequential 24-hour response to chosen scenario. Precise understanding of Australian consular support and consular limitations. Clear explanation of insurance claims and emergency funds access.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>3–4 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Logical action plan addressing the crisis scenario. Sound understanding of embassy assistance and travel insurance procedures.</p>
        </td>
        <td>
          <strong>1–2 Marks</strong>
          <p style="margin: 3px 0 0 0;">Vague or unrealistic response to crisis scenario. Incorrect assumptions regarding embassy financial support or insurance coverage.</p>
        </td>
        <td class="score-cell">/ 6</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Total Row -->
      <tr style="background:#f1f5f9; font-weight:bold; font-size:9.5pt;">
        <td colspan="4" style="text-align:right; text-transform:uppercase;">Total Score:</td>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-size:10pt;">/ 30</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <div class="rubric-title" style="margin-top: 0;">Performance Grade Breakdown</div>
  
  <table class="grade-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 8%; text-align:center;">Grade</th>
        <th style="width: 15%; text-align:center;">Mark Range</th>
        <th style="width: 77%;">Standard Descriptor</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="grade-cell">A</td>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold; font-size:9.5pt; vertical-align:middle;">26 – 30</td>
        <td>The student demonstrates extensive knowledge and understanding of travel planning, financial literacy, consumer rights, and risk management, displaying sophisticated research, comparative analysis, and problem-solving skills.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="grade-cell">B</td>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold; font-size:9.5pt; vertical-align:middle;">21 – 25</td>
        <td>The student demonstrates thorough knowledge and understanding of travel logistics and budgeting, displaying well-developed research, accurate currency calculations, and clear emergency planning.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="grade-cell">C</td>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold; font-size:9.5pt; vertical-align:middle;">15 – 20</td>
        <td>The student demonstrates sound knowledge and understanding of travel planning, completing all core sections within budget parameters with competent research and basic analysis.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="grade-cell">D</td>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold; font-size:9.5pt; vertical-align:middle;">8 – 14</td>
        <td>The student demonstrates basic knowledge of travel planning and budgeting, with limited research depth, partial costing, or incomplete emergency procedures.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="grade-cell">E</td>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold; font-size:9.5pt; vertical-align:middle;">0 – 7</td>
        <td>The student demonstrates elementary knowledge, with major components missing, inaccurate financial data, or failure to meet the task brief.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="feedback-section">
    <div class="feedback-title">Teacher Feedback &amp; Comments</div>
    <div style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
      <strong>Key Strengths:</strong>
      <div class="feedback-box" style="margin-top: 5px;">__________________________________________________________________________________________<br/>__________________________________________________________________________________________</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Areas for Improvement / Next Steps:</strong>
      <div class="feedback-box" style="margin-top: 5px;">__________________________________________________________________________________________<br/>__________________________________________________________________________________________</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table class="footer-signatures">
    <tr>
      <td style="border:none; padding: 0; width: 60%;">
        <strong>Assessor Signature:</strong> ____________________________________
      </td>
      <td style="border:none; padding: 0; width: 40%; text-align: right;">
        <strong>Date:</strong> ____ / ____ / 202__
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

</body>
</html>
